; Third audit: verify the corpus-backed realization movement after round two.
import "../form/form-stdlib/core.fk"
import "review-panel.fk"
import "review-ask.fk"

(ra-review
  "cognition/form-neutral-word-field-locales.fk"
  "Third adversarial verification only; do not edit any file. Read cognition/form-neutral-word-field-locales.fk, cognition/tests/form-neutral-word-field-locales-band.fk, and observe/form-neutral-word-field-locales-live.fk. The second review requested provenance inside detached records, resolvable source references, separate refusal witnesses, exact 61/30 counts, and removal of an unsupported NFC claim; those repairs are present. A later user clarification asks for neutral-symbol-first generation with minimal static data and maximal dynamic computation. Verify the new implementation without rewarding the word dynamic. The primary path must be neutral symbol -> candidate sense -> source policy -> indexed corpus lookup or local fragment recipe -> surface. fwfl-runtime must discover six corpus rows from neutral synset identities rather than English labels or duplicated numeric row indexes. Nineteen exact surfaces must now be read at runtime from the committed 10,000-concept multilingual substrate, leaving 72 locally character-complete lexical bridges: 52 multi-fragment, 20 single-anchor. There are still zero learned or productive morphology rules, and the file must say so plainly. Confirm all 91 generated surfaces remain exact, all exact identity roundtrips succeed, source counts remain 61 authored / 19 body corpus / 11 external, records remain nine fields, speaker review remains 91 unreviewed / 0 reviewed, matching means exact code-point identity with no normalization, and the fresh native band returns 8388607. Challenge the corpus index discovery, absent/invalid inputs, any accidental English pivot, source-reference consistency, and whether runtime corpus lookup is falsely presented as word generation from semantic geometry. Return PASS AS A BOUNDED NEUTRAL-SYMBOL-FIRST REALIZATION SEED, REVISE, or BLOCK, naming the smallest executable correction. Empty or unavailable panel doors are absence, never votes.")
